{"type":"message","id":"8f570b2f","parentId":"8404ed6e","timestamp":"2026-06-07T00:45:01.117Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API only shows MARKET orders (all FILLED). No STOP, STOP_MARKET, TAKE_PROFIT, or TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET orders anywhere in the history.\n\nBut the user says they can see 8 orders in the 委托 interface. This means the orders exist on the exchange but the API isn't returning them.\n\nThis could be because:\n1. On Binance Futures, TP/SL orders might be \"conditional orders\" that need a different API endpoint\n2. Or perhaps the orders are \"strategy orders\" on Binance\n\nActually, I think I know the issue. On Binance Futures, the standard `/fapi/v1/openOrders` and `/fapi/v1/allOrders` might not include conditional orders like STOP_MARKET and TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET. These might be under a different system.\n\nWait, actually they should be included. Let me check if maybe the order types on testnet are different.\n\nActually, I recall that Binance Futures has a concept of \"strategy orders\" or \"algo orders\" for TP/SL that are managed differently. Let me check...\n\nActually no, on Binance Futures, TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET and STOP_MARKET orders should appear in openOrders and allOrders. The fact that they don't appear is very strange.\n\nBut wait - the user says they CAN see them. This is a discrepancy between what the API returns and what the user sees. This could be a testnet quirk, or it could be that the orders are on the exchange web UI but the API key doesn't have permission to see them, or there's a data sync issue.\n\nActually, I just realized - maybe the problem is even simpler. On Binance Futures, TP/SL can be set as \"position TP/SL\" which are different from regular orders. They might not show up in `/fapi/v1/openOrders` but rather through position endpoints.\n\nLet me check the position information more carefully, specifically looking for `takeProfit` or `stopLoss` fields in the position risk response.\n\nAlso, I just realized I should check if the user's \"8 orders\" might be on a different exchange or if they're looking at something else entirely.\n\nLet me check the position detail for TP/SL settings.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_o60BItPRjm1TN3Qzuuyh4285","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport json, time, hmac, hashlib, requests\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlparse, urlencode\n\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\ncfg = bat._load_config_if_changed()['binance_api']\napi_key = cfg['api_key']\nsecret_key = cfg['secret_key']\n\ndef signed_get(path):\n    ts = int(time.time() * 1000)\n    parsed = urlparse('http://x' + path)\n    params = parse_qs(parsed.query)\n    flat = {k: v[0] for k, v in params.items() if v}\n    flat['timestamp'] = ts\n    qs = urlencode(sorted(flat.items()))\n    sig = hmac.new(secret_key.encode(), qs.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    url = f'{bat.BASE_URL}{parsed.path}?{qs}&signature={sig}'\n    r = requests.get(url, headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key}, timeout=15, verify=False)\n    return r.json()\n\n# 查仓位详情（v2 包含更多字段如 adl, 但不一定有 tp/sl）\ndata = signed_get('/fapi/v2/positionRisk')\nfor p in data:\n    amt = float(p.get('positionAmt', 0))\n    if amt == 0:\n        continue\n    print(f'{p[\\\"symbol\\\"]}: 仓位{amt}')\n    # 打印所有字段看看有没有 tp/sl\n    interesting = {k: v for k, v in p.items() if v and v != '0' and v != '0.0'}\n    print(f'  非空字段: {json.dumps(interesting)}')\n    print()\n\" 2>&1","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":978,"output":1413,"cacheRead":30720,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33111,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780793084942}}
