{"type":"message","id":"6a2c73b2","parentId":"b755829f","timestamp":"2026-06-07T00:45:18.429Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see - the position data from Binance Futures doesn't include TP/SL fields. Those are NOT embedded in the position object on Binance Futures.\n\nSo the user says they can see 8 orders in the 委托 interface. But the API shows 0 open orders and the history only shows MARKET orders. \n\nThis is really puzzling. Let me think about what could be going on:\n\n1. Perhaps the user is looking at a different account or different exchange\n2. Perhaps the TP/SL orders are on the Binance interface but the API key doesn't have permission to query them\n3. Perhaps there's a bug in my query\n\nActually wait - I just realized something. The orders might exist but my API key might not have the right permissions. Let me check the config again for permissions. The config says `permissions` might restrict certain order types.\n\nActually, let me just try a completely different approach. Let me look at this from the user's perspective. The user says they see 8 orders. My API says 0. Who's right?\n\nThe most likely explanation is:\n1. There ARE TP/SL orders on the exchange but the API isn't returning them for some testnet-specific reason\n2. Or the orders are a different type (like strategy/algo orders) that need a different API endpoint\n\nOn Binance Futures, there's a concept of \"strategy\" stop orders where you set TP/SL that are tied to the position. These might be shown differently on the web UI vs the API.\n\nActually, now I recall - on Binance Futures Testnet, there can be differences in how orders work. The testnet might not fully support certain order types.\n\nLet me just tell the user: my API queries show 0 open orders but if they can see 8 orders on the Binance web interface, then the orders exist. The API might just not be showing them properly (testnet quirk). The important thing is the user can see them. Let me acknowledge this discrepancy and confirm the user is right.\n\nActually wait, I should try one more thing - let me look at the binance_auto_trade.py to see how it places TP/SL orders, because maybe it uses a different API endpoint for conditional orders.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_WGd4aS9Qldm2ZzrpDlWs3173","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n -i \"stop\\|take_profit\\|tp_\\|sl_\\|trailing\\|订单类型\" ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py | head -30","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1034,"output":1029,"cacheRead":32512,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34575,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780793106501}}
