{"type":"message","id":"240c1992","parentId":"7ecdac50","timestamp":"2026-06-07T00:51:02.234Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's already a `cancel_algo_orders` function that queries `/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders`. Let me look at the `request` function to understand how API calls work, so I can build a similar function in query_positions.py.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, the `bat` module has a `request` function. Let me check if I can just call `bat.request` or the `cancel_algo_orders` function returns the algo orders list.\n\nWait, but `cancel_algo_orders` takes a symbol and cancels all open algo orders for that symbol. It doesn't return them in a useful format.\n\nI think the cleanest approach is to just add a helper function in `query_positions.py` that:\n1. Calls the Binance API directly for openAlgoOrders (reusing the same API key/signature logic)\n2. Or better yet, extract the basic request/signature logic into a shared helper\n\nActually, looking at the bat module, let me check if there's a way to list open algo orders without cancelling them. Let me look at the request function.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_hvrPoGNlkgYLoBIiuwdn8441","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"^def request\\|def signed_get\\|def _sign\" ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py | head -10","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":170,"output":562,"cacheRead":42880,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43612,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780793455659}}
