{"type":"message","id":"7d9e9420","parentId":"111acd6d","timestamp":"2026-06-07T02:13:13.322Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_Qv1SP9mfBvN4c8AothYy2334","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 八、熔断器\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nclass CircuitBreaker:\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.daily_pnl   = 0.0\n        self.reset_date  = datetime.now().date()\n        self.paused_until: Optional[datetime] = None\n\n    def record_trade(self, pnl: float):\n        today = datetime.now().date()\n        if today != self.reset_date:\n            self.daily_pnl = 0.0\n            self.reset_date = today\n            self.consecutive_losses = 0  # 每日重置连亏计数\n        self.daily_pnl += pnl\n\n        # 连亏计数\n        if pnl < 0:\n            self.consecutive_losses = getattr(self, 'consecutive_losses', 0) + 1\n            if self.consecutive_losses >= 3:\n                self.paused_until = datetime.now() + timedelta(hours=2)\n                log.warning(f\"⚠️ 连亏{self.consecutive_losses}次，暂停 2 小时\")\n                self.consecutive_losses = 0\n        else:\n            self.consecutive_losses = 0  # 盈利重置\n\n    def is_trading_allowed(self) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n        # 2026-03-31 22:07 老公指示：清除熔断\n        self.paused_until = None\n        self.consecutive_losses = 0\n        # 检查暂停\n        if self.paused_until and datetime.now() < self.paused_until:\n            remain = int((self.paused_until - datetime.now()).total_seconds() / 60)\n            return False, f\"熔断中，还需 {remain} 分钟\"\n\n        # 检查日亏损\n        loss_pct = self.daily_pnl / CONFIG[\"total_capital\"]\n        if loss_pct < CONFIG[\"circuit_breaker_pct\"]:\n            self.paused_until = datetime.now() + timedelta(hours=CONFIG[\"circuit_breaker_hours\"])\n            msg = f\"⚠️ 熔断！日亏损 {loss_pct:.1%}，暂停 {CONFIG['circuit_breaker_hours']} 小时\"\n            log.warning(msg)\n            write_alert(msg)\n            return False, msg\n\n        return True, \"ok\"\n\n\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# 九、信号冷却\n\n[1912 more lines in file. Use offset=878 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780798393304}}
{"type":"message","id":"60ef85d5","parentId":"7d9e9420","timestamp":"2026-06-07T02:13:24.673Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting. There's a line that says \"2026-03-31 22:07 老公指示：清除熔断\" - this means the circuit breaker was intentionally disabled on 老公's orders.\n\nSo the circuit breaker:\n1. Was previously disabled by 老公's instruction (line 856-857: clears paused_until and consecutive_losses)\n2. BUT the daily loss check still exists (line 865-873): if loss_pct < CONFIG[\"circuit_breaker_pct\"] (-10%), it triggers a pause\n\nWait, let me re-read. The `is_trading_allowed` method:\n1. First clears the paused_until (line 856-857) \n2. Then checks if paused (line 860-862) - this will never be true since it was just cleared\n3. Then checks daily loss (line 865-873) - this can trigger a new pause\n\nSo even though the old pause state is cleared every time, the daily loss check can still trigger a new one. With daily_pnl = -11.49 and total_capital = 100, loss_pct = -0.1149, which is less than -0.10, so a new circuit breaker should trigger.\n\nBUT the clear at lines 856-857 happens EVERY CALL to is_trading_allowed, so:\n1. Call 1: clear old state → check daily loss → daily_pnl = -11.49 → trigger pause → set paused_until\n2. Call 2: clear state (including newly set paused_until!) → check daily loss → daily_pnl = -11.49 → trigger pause → set paused_until AGAIN\n3. ...this loops forever, always triggering but also always clearing\n\nWait, that means the circuit breaker is effectively partially broken. Every call to `is_trading_allowed()` will:\n1. Clear paused_until\n2. Daily loss is still > 10% → trigger new pause → but this pause gets cleared on next call\n\nSo the monitor would refuse trades every time (returning False with the message), but the \"pause\" timer never actually counts down. It's like a permanent reject until daily_pnl recovers.\n\nBut let me check if the monitor actually calls `is_trading_allowed` before opening positions...","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ji4qar88j7Z01FmxgDKr3289","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"is_trading_allowed\\|circuit_breaker\\|breaker\" ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py | head -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":652,"output":1056,"cacheRead":55808,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57516,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780798393334}}
{"type":"message","id":"829dcd27","parentId":"60ef85d5","timestamp":"2026-06-07T02:13:24.854Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_ji4qar88j7Z01FmxgDKr3289","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"99:    \"circuit_breaker_pct\": -0.10,   # 日亏损超10%触发\n100:    \"circuit_breaker_hours\": 4,     # 暂停4小时\n855:    def is_trading_allowed(self) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n866:        if loss_pct < CONFIG[\"circuit_breaker_pct\"]:\n867:            self.paused_until = datetime.now() + timedelta(hours=CONFIG[\"circuit_breaker_hours\"])\n868:            msg = f\"⚠️ 熔断！日亏损 {loss_pct:.1%}，暂停 {CONFIG['circuit_breaker_hours']} 小时\"\n2223:    circuit_breaker  = CircuitBreaker()\n2347:    realized_pnl = restore_daily_pnl(circuit_breaker)\n2348:    # 熔断暂停仅由 is_trading_allowed 管理，不再在启动时清零 daily_pnl\n2349:    circuit_breaker.paused_until = None\n2350:    circuit_breaker.consecutive_losses = 0\n2490:                circuit_breaker.record_trade(pnl)\n2587:                allowed, reason = circuit_breaker.is_trading_allowed()\n2759:                    positions, prices, indicators, circuit_breaker, fg_cache, indicator_engine\n2769:                \"daily_pnl\":   circuit_breaker.daily_pnl,"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":109,"aggregated":"99:    \"circuit_breaker_pct\": -0.10,   # 日亏损超10%触发\n100:    \"circuit_breaker_hours\": 4,     # 暂停4小时\n855:    def is_trading_allowed(self) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n866:        if loss_pct < CONFIG[\"circuit_breaker_pct\"]:\n867:            self.paused_until = datetime.now() + timedelta(hours=CONFIG[\"circuit_breaker_hours\"])\n868:            msg = f\"⚠️ 熔断！日亏损 {loss_pct:.1%}，暂停 {CONFIG['circuit_breaker_hours']} 小时\"\n2223:    circuit_breaker  = CircuitBreaker()\n2347:    realized_pnl = restore_daily_pnl(circuit_breaker)\n2348:    # 熔断暂停仅由 is_trading_allowed 管理，不再在启动时清零 daily_pnl\n2349:    circuit_breaker.paused_until = None\n2350:    circuit_breaker.consecutive_losses = 0\n2490:                circuit_breaker.record_trade(pnl)\n2587:                allowed, reason = circuit_breaker.is_trading_allowed()\n2759:                    positions, prices, indicators, circuit_breaker, fg_cache, indicator_engine\n2769:                \"daily_pnl\":   circuit_breaker.daily_pnl,","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780798404844}}
{"type":"message","id":"a1f90fc1","parentId":"829dcd27","timestamp":"2026-06-07T02:13:33.609Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so:\n- `circuit_breaker = CircuitBreaker()` is created at line 2223\n- `is_trading_allowed()` is called at line 2587 before opening new positions\n- The issue is that lines 856-857 clear the paused_until EVERY TIME the method is called\n\nSo the flow is:\n1. Daily PnL hits -11.49, exceeding -10%\n2. Every time the monitor tries to open a position, `is_trading_allowed()` is called\n3. It clears paused_until, then immediately sees daily loss > 10% and sets a new pause\n4. Returns False, preventing new trades\n\nThis means the monitor IS blocking new trades, but the \"4 hour pause\" doesn't actually count down because it gets cleared every cycle. It's effectively a permanent block until daily PnL recovers or the counter resets at midnight.\n\nSo the circuit breaker is working-ish - it blocks new trades. Just the timer part is broken because of the forced clear at line 856-857.\n\nLet me check the recent monitor logs to confirm it's actually being triggered.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_tK7TYvHEsuEPDXlFaY9h0749","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport subprocess, sys\n# 查看 monitor 最近的日志输出\nresult = subprocess.run(['tail', '-150', '/tmp/crypto_monitor_*.log'], capture_output=True, text=True, shell=True)\nprint(result.stdout[-3000:] if result.stdout else 'no match')\n\" 2>&1; echo \"===\"; ls -la /tmp/crypto_monitor* 2>/dev/null; echo \"===\"; journalctl -u crypto-monitor --no-pager -n 30 2>/dev/null || echo \"no journalctl\"","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":402,"output":664,"cacheRead":56960,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":58026,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":